- CAPTURE MEASURES THE MIX'S ENVELOPE ONCE, AND THE EXPORT STOPPED MEASURING IT AGAIN (X1,
  2026-08-26). O2 kept three scalars from the capture-time accumulator and SORTED the window series
  away; the series is now kept IN TIME ORDER on `Recording.loudness.envelope` (windowRms + windowPeak
  + the window length + the recording-timeline ms of window 0). 121 KB per 30 minutes. A percentile is
  a statistic of a multiset, so an EDIT is a SELECTION of those windows — no second decode of every
  audio channel to rebuild them. Three consumers, all measured on the rigs:
    · the RENDER'S EDITED export — RenderStats.probeDecodes reads 0 with the envelope and 2 without,
      p90 within 0.267 dB of the probe, and the APPLIED MAKEUP GAIN identical (0.000 dB);
    · SMART CUT, which copies its video packets and finished in under a second and then paid a full
      audio decode anyway — its own comment said the capture shortcut could not describe a cut, which
      was true of the scalars and false of the envelope;
    · F5a TIGHTEN — the production analyzeSilence, run twice on one take, proposes THE SAME TWO CUTS
      (0 ms boundary delta, threshold identical) in 1 ms instead of 70. The probe costs ~147 ms per
      minute of audio, so Tighten on a 30-minute take goes from ~4.4 s to ~1 ms.
  FENCES, each one a case where the stored windows describe a signal the file will not carry, all
  returning null so the caller probes exactly as before: no envelope (a take recorded before X1 is
  bit-for-bit unchanged) · a channel set that is not what capture summed · a PER-CHANNEL trim · a SPED
  span (F5b retimes the material) · fewer than 30 whole windows · and the p20 codec-floor guard, which
  generalizes unchanged and is now one shared function. F5a takes narrower fences still — ONE kept
  span, because the analyser indexes windows by OUTPUT position — and pads with zero-RMS windows
  wherever the output has no audio, which is precisely the digital silence the probe measures there.
  KNOWN EXPOSURE, stated because no rig reaches it: capture measures PCM and the probe measures the
  DECODED file, and a codec removes content below its perceptual floor (O2 measured up to 15 dB apart
  down there). On the known-silence rig the two floors agree to 0.04 dB; a take whose room tone sits
