- THE LIMITER'S FOLD IS ALGEBRAIC u/(1+u), NOT tanh (2026-08-23). tanh scaled by (1-knee)=0.05 saturates
  to full scale at an input of 1.152, while the makeup gain was licensed to reach 1.9 — so a 1.66:1 range
  of the loudest content collapsed onto ONE 16-bit code and every boosted transient came out as a bare
  impulse (measured in a PO take: 217 full-scale ~0.25 ms spikes from t=12.5s, heard as crackle). The
  algebraic fold keeps f(0)=0, f'(0)=1 (C1 knee, normal program untouched) and f(inf)=1, but approaches
  the ceiling polynomially and stays resolved to LIMIT_USABLE_MAX ~= 82. Below the knee it is bit-identical.
